<worksheet>
  <title>Quiz: Simple and Compound Interest Attempt 1</title>
  <introduction>    
    <p>
      Name: <fillin characters="45"/>
    </p>
    <assemblage>
      <p>
        <md>
          A = P(1 + rt) \qquad
          A = P\left(1 + \frac{r}{n}\right)^{nt} \qquad
          I = A - P
        </md>
      </p>
    </assemblage>
  </introduction>
  
  <exercise workspace="0.8in">
    <statement>
      <p>Suppose you pay back $340 on a $300 loan. You had the loan for 90 days. What simple annual interest rate did you pay?</p>
      <p>Use the Bankers' Rule that 1 year = 360 days. Round to the nearest hundredth of a percent (two decimal places).</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
  
  <exercise workspace="0.8in">
    <statement>
      <p>To fund a community garden project, Terrence received a sustainability loan of $1,150. The loan accrues simple interest at an annual rate of 4.7% and must be repaid in 8 years. How much interest will Terrence owe in addition to the original $1,150?</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
  
  <exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>You deposit $2,000 in an account earning 3% annual interest compounded monthly. How much will you have in the account in 10 years?</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
  
  <exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>Melissa deposits $900 in an account earning 5% annual interest compounded annually. How much will Melissa have in the account after 12 years? How much interest will Melissa have earned?</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
</worksheet>
